Package: FuzzyMFD
Type: Package
Title: Membership Functions, Fuzzification and Defuzzification
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-11-24
Authors@R:
    person("Mohamad Yamen", "AL Mohamad",
           email = "yamenmohamad@tabrizu.ac.ir",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-1665-7203"))
Description: Implements the methods of T. J. Ross (2000) "Membership
    Functions, Fuzzification and Defuzzification", in P. S. Szczepaniak,
    P. J. G. Lisboa and J. Kacprzyk (eds.), Fuzzy Systems in Medicine,
    Springer-Verlag, Berlin Heidelberg, 49-78. Fuzzy sets on the real line are stored as exact
    piecewise-linear membership functions. The package provides standard
    membership function shapes; the features of a membership function
    (core, support, boundaries, height, normality, convexity, crossover
    points, prototype); exact union, intersection and complement;
    fuzzification of crisp readings; membership value assignment by rank
    ordering of pairwise preferences and by inductive reasoning with
    entropy minimisation (primary, secondary and tertiary thresholds and
    the resulting partitions); and defuzzification by the max-membership,
    centroid, weighted-average and mean-max methods. The worked examples
    of the chapter are included as data and example sets.
